{"config":{"lang":["en"],"separator":"[\\s\\-]+","pipeline":["stopWordFilter"]},"docs":[{"location":"","title":"Welcome to My blog","text":"<p>I created this blog to share my thoughts, learnings, and experiences with you.</p>"},{"location":"#what-do-you-want-to-explore-today","title":"What do you want to explore today?","text":"<p>Here are the topics I plan to write about:</p> <ul> <li>Chess</li> </ul> <p>Quick hits on tactics, patterns, and ideas. No theory dumps\u2014just what sticks and wins games.</p> <p>You can find my chess.com page here.</p> <ul> <li>Verification</li> </ul> <p>Notes on many things related to Design Verification and relevant gotchas.</p> <ul> <li>Philosophy</li> </ul> <p>Snippets of old-school wisdom. Nothing preachy\u2014just thoughts worth chewing on.</p> <p>I hope you find this blog interesting and informative. Cheers!</p> <p>Side Note: The picture I used on this page, is a caveman sharing his learnings. It is supposed to metaphorically represent me sharing my understandings through this blog!</p>"},{"location":"blog/","title":"Blog","text":""},{"location":"blog/posts/hello-world/","title":"Hello world!","text":"<p>Most popular phrase used when trying out new stuff :P</p>","tags":["Hello","World"]},{"location":"blog/posts/chess_chronicles/chess_index/","title":"\u201cAt the end of the game, the king and the pawn go back in the same box\u201d","text":"<ul> <li>My Games</li> <li>Pro Games Study</li> <li>Openings Repertoires</li> <li>Middle Game Strategies</li> <li>Endgame Techniques</li> <li>Tactics and Motifs</li> </ul> <p>Side Note: If you're curious about the picture I used on this page, it's an enlightened pawn that puzzles a horse.</p>","tags":["Chess/Index Pages"]},{"location":"blog/posts/chess_chronicles/end_game_study/endgame_index/","title":"Standard Combinations","text":"","tags":["Chess/Basics"]},{"location":"blog/posts/chess_chronicles/middle_game_strats/midgame_index/","title":"Beginner's Guide to Imbalances","text":"","tags":["C