an/#accelerated-dragon","title":"Accelerated Dragon","text":"","tags":["Chess/Openings"]},{"location":"blog/posts/chess_chronicles/openings/White/italian/","title":"Italian Game","text":"","tags":["Chess/Openings"]},{"location":"blog/posts/chess_chronicles/openings/White/kings_gambit/","title":"King's Gambit","text":"","tags":["Chess/Openings"]},{"location":"blog/posts/chess_chronicles/openings/White/scotch/","title":"Scotch Game","text":"","tags":["Chess/Openings"]},{"location":"blog/posts/chess_chronicles/openings/White/vienna/","title":"Vienna Game","text":"","tags":["Chess/Openings"]},{"location":"blog/posts/chess_chronicles/pro_games/progames_index/","title":"My style","text":"","tags":["Chess/Games"]},{"location":"blog/posts/chess_chronicles/tactics_and_motifs/tactics_index/","title":"Basic Tactics","text":"","tags":["Chess/Study"]},{"location":"blog/posts/verification_files/verification_index/","title":"\"The trust of the innocent is the liar's most useful tool.\"","text":"<ul> <li>Bootstrapping Verification</li> </ul>","tags":["Index Pages"]},{"location":"blog/posts/verification_files/bootstrapping_verification/1_Verification_with_Verilog/","title":"Table of Contents","text":"<ul> <li>Why are we doing verification with Verilog?</li> <li>4-bit Counter DUT Verification</li> <li>wire vs. reg</li> <li>Blocking vs. Non-blocking</li> <li>Synchronous vs. Asynchronous</li> <li>Verification Plan</li> <li>Manual Verification</li> <li>Test Bench</li> <li>256-bit Counter DUT Verification</li> <li>Verification Plan</li> <li>Manual Verification</li> <li>Test Bench</li> <li>Tasks and Functions</li> <li>System Tasks and Functions</li> </ul>"},{"location":"blog/posts/verification_files/bootstrapping_verification/1_Verification_with_Verilog/#why-are-we-doing-verification-with-verilog","title":"Why are we doing verification with Verilog?","text":""},{"location":"blog/posts/verification_files/bootstrapping_verification/1_Verification_with_Verilog/#4-bit-counter-dut-verification